**Task Model – Concrete Actions**

| Task ID | Task Title | Text (justification) | Relation | Location | Number of Robots |
|---------|------------|-----------------------|----------|----------|------------------|
| AT1 | **Navigate to Storage** | *Perform* moving the robot to the storage location where resources are found. | AND | Storage | `[1,n]` |
| AT2 | **Send Request Message** | *Perform* sending a precise specification of requested resources to the storage. | AND | Storage | `[1,n]` |
| AT3 | **Wait for Retrieval** | *Perform* waiting until the storage has retrieved the resources. | AND | Storage | `[1,n]` |
| AT4 | **Monitor Battery Level (10%)** | *Perform* continuous battery monitoring; if below 10 % trigger low‑battery handling. | AND | Robot’s current location | `[1,n]` |
| AT5 | **Go to Recharge Station** | *Perform* navigating the robot to the nearest recharge station. | AND | RechargeStation | `[1,n]` |
| AT6 | **Assign Mission to Another Robot** | *Perform* notifying central control to assign the mission to another robot. | AND | CentralControl | `[1,n]` |
| AT7 | **Navigate to Storage** | *Perform* moving the robot to storage to pick up resources. | AND | Storage | `[1,n]` |
| AT8 | **Pick Up Resources** | *Perform* loading resources onto the robot. | AND | Storage | `[1,n]` |
| AT9 | **Deliver to Destination** | *Perform* transporting resources to the specified destination location. | AND | Destination | `[1,n]` |
| AT11 | **Return Resource to Checkpoint** | *Perform* returning the resource to a checkpoint when battery is low. | AND | Checkpoint | `[1,n]` |
| AT12 | **Assign Remaining Task to Another Robot** | *Perform* notifying central control to assign the remaining task to another robot. | AND | Checkpoint | `[1,n]` |
| AT13 | **Trigger Alert and Send Report** | *Perform* triggering an alert and sending a report to the sector manager if the resource cannot be returned to a checkpoint. | AND | SectorManager | `[1,n]` |

---

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 → G2** (AND) – The mission starts with the collection phase.  
- **G2 → G3** (AND) – After collection, the delivery phase follows.  
- **G2.1 → G2** (AND) – Visit order determination precedes normal collection.  
- **G2.2 → G2** (AND) – Collection tasks (normal or low‑battery) are performed.  
- **G2.2a → G2.2** (AND) – Normal collection tasks.  
- **G2.2b → G2.2** (AND) – Low‑battery handling during collection.  
- **G3.1 → G3** (AND) – Delivery tasks (normal or low‑battery) are performed.  
- **G3.1a → G3.1** (AND) – Normal delivery tasks.  
- **G3.1b → G3.1** (AND) – Low‑battery handling during delivery.  
- **G3.2 → G3** (AND) – Failure handling for resource return.  

All tasks are linked to their parent goals with an **AND** relation, reflecting that each task must be executed for the goal to succeed. The runtime annotations (`;`, `#`, `FALLBACK`) capture the sequential, parallel, and fallback execution structures required by the mission description.
